1
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:11,410
With another man?

2
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:13,000
Seriously?

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,480
Is it anyone I know?

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,450
No.

5
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:23,310
He worked for a club
specializing in women's needs.

6
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:27,370
I happened to bump into him the other day.

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,650
A club?

8
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:35,560
I didn't realize the experience
meant so much to you.

9
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:40,000
I also questioned myself.

10
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:46,260
Was sex really so important to me?

11
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,230
But...

12
00:00:55,670 --> 00:01:02,000
I now know I'm a 31 year old woman
who can have proper wants.

13
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:08,430
Sorry.

14
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:12,540
That's not a revelation
to be proud of, is it?

15
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:18,220
I know you treated me well.

16
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:25,840
I'm so sorry I've hurt you.

17
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:32,250
[Divorce Forms]

18
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:38,380
I see. So you told Ouji everything.

19
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,800
Yeah.

20
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:47,010
Actually, same here.

21
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:48,380
Huh?

22
00:01:48,380 --> 00:01:50,250
I'll be getting a divorce.

23
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:51,740
What?

24
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:53,460
I told my husband everything.

25
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:56,020
L-Like, "everything"?

26
00:01:56,020 --> 00:02:00,640
Yup. We're discussing the arrangements
as we speak.

27
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:05,190
What will happen to Chizuka?

28
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:08,830
We'll be fighting over her custody.

29
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:12,460
But I'll be paying him
a settlement fee regardless.

30
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:15,110
I see.

31
00:02:15,110 --> 00:02:23,060
Everyone's making serious confessions, huh?

32
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:27,400
You started it, Akina.

33
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,350
Yeah.

34
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,080
Huh?

35
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:35,310
Watching your honorable confession

36
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,300
lit a fire in my heart.

37
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,040
Honorable...

38
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,730
That's one way to put it.

39
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:49,650
My confession was far from honorable.

40
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:57,490
I saw how Ouji treasured our relationship,

41
00:02:57,490 --> 00:03:01,240
and knew I couldn't keep secrets anymore.

42
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:03,770
[Finale]

43
00:04:03,770 --> 00:04:06,570
[Saint Love Survivors]

44
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:11,520
[What lies after a "happy end"?]

45
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:19,000
A divorce.

46
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,050
Excuse us.

47
00:04:24,050 --> 00:04:26,260
Kazahaya is ready for you.

48
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:30,240
Good morning.
I'll be your makeup artist for today.

49
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,180
Good morning.

50
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:38,820
Fuyumi.

51
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,470
Is it true you got divorced?

52
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:51,210
We're still fighting over it.

53
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:01,400
I'm so sorry.

54
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:05,150
I...

55
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:09,940
I logically knew it was wrong.

56
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:14,110
But couldn't talk myself out of it.

57
00:05:17,590 --> 00:05:20,660
And now, I've messed up your family.

58
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:24,820
Shota, I already had issues with my husband.

59
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:30,070
Meeting you just gave me the resolve
to file a divorce.

60
00:05:33,030 --> 00:05:37,610
I'm sorry to make you feel responsible.

61
00:05:42,470 --> 00:05:44,120
But, I...

62
00:05:49,010 --> 00:05:52,640
No crying before an important shoot.

63
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:57,040
Raise your head.

64
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:05,420
You're an actor, right?

65
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:11,840
Use that to your advantage.

66
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:46,350
I had sex with another man.

67
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,380
Why?

68
00:07:14,490 --> 00:07:16,040
Haru!

69
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:30,600
That's NTR, right?

70
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:31,520
Huh?

71
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,040
"Netorare".

72
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,800
When you get excited seeing your girl

73
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,050
get it on with another guy.

74
00:07:38,050 --> 00:07:39,980
The hell? Is that a kink?

75
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:44,330
Can be. It helps reignite some couples, too.

76
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:46,100
Maybe your friend's in a similar boat?

77
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:50,000
Well... Who knows.

78
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:53,220
But in the case of NTR,

79
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:58,230
the guy isn't looking at their partner
until she's taken, right?

80
00:07:58,230 --> 00:07:59,540
He's disrespecting his girl.

81
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:01,220
There you are.

82
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,720
Keiko. You here for a shoot?

83
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,740
Yeah. The livestream just ended.

84
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:07,860
I was looking everywhere for you.

85
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:11,610
Maybe I was disrespecting her.

86
00:08:12,170 --> 00:08:13,120
Huh?

87
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,800
I thought being with her would be easy.

88
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,620
She was cute.

89
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:20,900
She wouldn't make romance a pain.

90
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:25,410
I thought she would always love me.

91
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:30,030
The cool guy she's come to know.

92
00:08:33,810 --> 00:08:35,830
I'm so lame.

93
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:39,080
And for our lame narcissist, I have a gift.

94
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:40,900
Hey, that's that popular novel.

95
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,020
Does Ouji even read?

96
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,820
I'm not interested in books, or fads.

97
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,540
Just read it.

98
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:49,830
I can't believe I'm pulling an assist.

99
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,200
But we'll call it even here.

100
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:54,230
What does that... Hey!

101
00:08:58,150 --> 00:09:00,600
[Saint Love Survivors]

102
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,990
This is...

103
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:22,220
<i>I made a prayer to God.</i>

104
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:26,780
<i>I didn't care what role I played in his life.</i>

105
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:32,490
<i>I simply wanted to be a part of it.</i>

106
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:37,670
<i>But that is most likely where our marriage...</i>

107
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:41,810
"Went wrong".

108
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,240
[Ouji]

109
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,540
[Haru, I read your book]
[I want to see you]

110
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:11,700
<i>The book... Like, my book?</i>

111
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:15,140
<i>H-How did he find out?</i>

112
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:17,040
[I want to see you]

113
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:22,530
He's going to ask for a divorce.

114
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:24,650
[This weekend, Izu. How about it?]

115
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:28,150
Huh? Izu?

116
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:34,840
[Izu-Kogen Station]

117
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,400
I came here with the guys once.

118
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,940
Huh?

119
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:53,620
It's a bit cliche, but it's a nice place.

120
00:10:56,170 --> 00:11:02,000
But... Why Izu?

121
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,110
I wanted to visit a hot spring, remember?

122
00:11:04,110 --> 00:11:06,650
I do, but...

123
00:11:07,390 --> 00:11:10,580
Wait, we're staying overnight?

124
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,030
Yeah.

125
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:14,330
Oh, don't worry. The inn has most amenities.

126
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:16,730
That's not why I'm confused.

127
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:23,450
Aren't we... getting a divorce?

128
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:25,600
- I wonder.
- Huh?

129
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,650
Come on, let's go.

130
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:32,600
There, I got a big one.

131
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,200
Nice.

132
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,480
Which one next...

133
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,400
Your crepe, sir.

134
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:06,240
[Inatori Akao Hotel]

135
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:18,430
I'm glad you're looking better.

136
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:38,140
Should we visit the inner garden?

137
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:39,420
Huh?

138
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:48,560
It sure gets chilly at night.

139
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,440
Want an extra layer?

140
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:51,710
Why?

141
00:12:51,710 --> 00:12:53,060
Huh?

142
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:56,150
I know you're mad.

143
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,280
I know you're in disbelief.

144
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:02,020
- Huh?
- Don't avoid the subject.

145
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,940
You read the book, didn't you?

146
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:09,890
I did.

147
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:12,760
- Then why...
- At first, I was stunned.

148
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:15,500
You didn't even tell me you were an author.

149
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:17,260
Sure, you didn't give exact names,

150
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,410
but did you really need to detail everything?

151
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:24,490
Sorry.

152
00:13:26,030 --> 00:13:31,040
One particular passage
shook me more than anything.

153
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:40,560
"That is most likely
where our marriage went wrong".

154
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:50,430
You said every decision you made, was wrong.

155
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,140
No, well...

156
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:59,820
That's a "me" problem.

157
00:14:05,390 --> 00:14:09,530
Entertaining book, though.

158
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:11,300
Huh?

159
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:14,740
Your book.

160
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:20,770
Maybe that's not much,

161
00:14:20,770 --> 00:14:25,200
coming from a guy who doesn't read.

162
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:29,210
But at some point,
I stopped caring about the whodunits,

163
00:14:29,210 --> 00:14:30,990
and let myself get absorbed in the story.

164
00:14:31,690 --> 00:14:34,390
It's like I joined the protagonist
on her adventure.

165
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:38,380
I learned you're an amazing individual, Haru.

166
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:45,090
Guess what I learned on my second read?

167
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:49,460
This guy is objectively the worst.

168
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:50,490
He's an idiot.

169
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:51,820
No, that's not...

170
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:54,050
I'm an idiot, too.

171
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:57,320
I'm an idiot,

172
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,410
but even I can tell.

173
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:06,840
This book's a love letter.

174
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:13,940
I can't believe you had so much to say.

175
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:22,860
You still love me, don't you?

176
00:15:27,950 --> 00:15:29,790
What the heck?

177
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,840
You assume I "still love you"?

178
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:39,710
Isn't that obvious?

179
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,810
Of course I still love you.

180
00:15:46,710 --> 00:15:48,360
I love your face.

181
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:51,180
I love your voice, mannerisms, tobacco scent,

182
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,700
bony hands, and the way you wear your boots.

183
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:01,010
But...

184
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,870
What I truly,

185
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:09,810
really love about you...

186
00:16:14,340 --> 00:16:18,810
Is that you don't doubt my love for you.

187
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:26,250
Your honestly dense kindness

188
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:31,810
has accepted me, time and time again.

189
00:16:34,810 --> 00:16:37,000
Despite how pathetic a person

190
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:41,840
I actually am.

191
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,040
No, I...

192
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,680
I haven't treated you well at all.

193
00:17:01,650 --> 00:17:03,840
You're an idiot.

194
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:06,720
You're happy I don't question your love?

195
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:10,560
I really am a narcissist.

196
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,790
Well, that's...

197
00:17:13,830 --> 00:17:19,230
How can you love me, when I'm so lame?

198
00:17:23,890 --> 00:17:25,620
I'm sorry.

199
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:31,590
I'm sorry I made you think you were pathetic.

200
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:36,590
I'm sorry I made you cry.

201
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:51,400
Maybe our marriage did go wrong.

202
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:55,180
But...

203
00:17:57,350 --> 00:17:59,450
We can still right our wrongs, right?

204
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:29,660
This trip is our official honeymoon.

205
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:50,640
What the... is this another one of my dreams?

206
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:53,600
Huh? No. This is real.

207
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:55,490
What?

208
00:18:55,490 --> 00:18:57,500
You okay?

209
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:00,820
What about you? Are you okay?

210
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:05,750
I actually really want to do it.

211
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:07,520
With you, specifically.

212
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,830
Huh?

213
00:19:08,830 --> 00:19:16,590
Actually, the other night I, uh...
had a reaction for once.

214
00:19:16,590 --> 00:19:18,470
Wanna know why?

215
00:19:20,670 --> 00:19:23,610
You had a dream, about me?

216
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:29,340
Apparently it happens.
It's called NTR, or something.

217
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,250
Perv.

218
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:38,890
But I've felt dreamy
seeing you do it out back

219
00:19:38,890 --> 00:19:42,780
with a complete stranger, too.

220
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:45,050
What? When did that happen?

221
00:19:45,050 --> 00:19:47,850
I guess we're a pair of perverts, huh?

222
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,820
You can say that again.

223
00:20:57,350 --> 00:20:59,470
I can get it in part way.

224
00:20:59,470 --> 00:21:02,230
Damn it, this is so frustrating.

225
00:21:02,230 --> 00:21:04,000
Don't be so hard on yourself.

226
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:07,580
I felt really good.

227
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:12,070
But I have to show up Mr. Delivery Guy.

228
00:21:12,070 --> 00:21:13,770
Aw...

229
00:21:13,770 --> 00:21:15,300
Here, I have an idea.

230
00:21:18,950 --> 00:21:21,300
Let me put in some effort.

231
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:27,230
No, I...

232
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:30,090
I'll put in my effort, too.

233
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:35,370
Wait, morning already?

234
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:40,400
Wow...

235
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:43,070
The sun's already coming up.

236
00:21:45,170 --> 00:21:47,370
It's 5AM in the morning.

237
00:21:47,370 --> 00:21:49,530
Which means I lasted 6 hours.

238
00:21:49,530 --> 00:21:54,020
At least I outdid him on time.

239
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:56,340
That's amazing.

240
00:21:57,250 --> 00:22:03,560
If we don't go all the way,
we can mess around forever.

241
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:16,560
Haru.

242
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:19,300
I love you.

243
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,850
Marry me?

244
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:28,460
Too bad. We already are, dummy.

245
00:22:34,070 --> 00:22:34,970
[One year later]

246
00:22:34,970 --> 00:22:37,200
Fuyumi.

247
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:40,980
Congratulations on the divorce!

248
00:22:40,980 --> 00:22:43,920
I can't believe it ended, just like that.

249
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:47,350
It helped that he found
another partner for himself.

250
00:22:47,350 --> 00:22:51,970
An assistant 15 years his junior, right?
What a shocker.

251
00:22:52,470 --> 00:22:54,340
How's your love life going, Akina?

252
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:58,910
Actually...

253
00:22:58,910 --> 00:23:02,080
I've begun seeing someone, sort of.

254
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:04,260
That's news to me.

255
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:06,650
- Who is it?
- He's a normal guy.

256
00:23:06,650 --> 00:23:09,730
A coworker who confessed to me.

257
00:23:09,730 --> 00:23:13,040
Nothing bad with normal, I guess.

258
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:18,870
He looks... kind.

259
00:23:18,870 --> 00:23:21,440
You're allowed to say he looks bland.

260
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:25,570
We did finally have sex, though.

261
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:28,410
Also normal, by the way.

262
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:31,370
Your standards are just way too high.

263
00:23:31,370 --> 00:23:32,910
You can't compare him to a professional.

264
00:23:32,910 --> 00:23:37,950
Aw, but I gave him the time to be pent up.

265
00:23:39,630 --> 00:23:43,330
We're sort of all like survivors.

266
00:23:43,330 --> 00:23:44,670
Survivors?

267
00:23:44,670 --> 00:23:46,610
Survivors of love.

268
00:23:48,380 --> 00:23:51,750
We each had our trials and tribulations,

269
00:23:51,750 --> 00:23:53,640
<i>but we all fought through it, together.</i>

270
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,050
<i>A survivor...</i>

271
00:23:55,050 --> 00:23:58,070
<i>That is what we are, yeah.</i>

272
00:23:59,550 --> 00:24:02,440
How is your love life going, Haru?

273
00:24:21,390 --> 00:24:23,000
Morning.

274
00:24:43,530 --> 00:24:47,030
[Saint Love Survivors]
